n .9in 1.1in 1.4in 1.6in 1.9in 2.1in 2.4in 2.6in 2.9in 3.1in 3.4in 3.6in 3.9in 4.1in'><span\r\nstyle='font-size:12.0pt;mso-bidi-font-size:10.0pt;font-family:\"Times New Roman\"'><span\r\nstyle='mso-tab-count:1'>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span><b style='mso-bidi-font-weight:normal'>67:46:13:10.&nbsp;&nbsp;Determining\r\nfamily size -- TMB.</b> Repealed. <o:p></o:p></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify;tab-stops:.4in .6in .9in 1.1in 1.4in 1.6in 1.9in 2.1in 2.4in 2.6in 2.9in 3.1in 3.4in 3.6in 3.9in 4.1in'><span\r\nstyle='font-size:12.0pt;mso-bidi-font-size:10.0pt;font-family:\"Times New Roman\"'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify;tab-stops:.4in .6in .9in 1.1in 1.4in 1.6in 1.9in 2.1in 2.4in 2.6in 2.9in 3.1in 3.4in 3.6in 3.9in 4.1in'><span\r\nstyle='font-size:12.0pt;mso-bidi-font-size:10.0pt;font-family:\"Times New Roman\"'><span\r\nstyle='mso-tab-count:1'>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span><b style='mso-bidi-font-weight:normal'>Source:</b>\r\n24 SDR 24, effective August 31, 1997; repealed, 36 SDR 215, effective July 1,\r\n2010.<o:p></o:p></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal style='text-align:justify;tab-stops:.4in .6in .9in 1.1in 1.4in 1.6in 1.9in 2.1in 2.4in 2.6in 2.9in 3.1in 3.4in 3.6in 3.9in 4.1in'><span\r\nstyle='font-size:12.0pt;mso-bidi-font-size:10.0pt;font-family:\"Times New Roman\"'><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p>\r\n\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n</body>\r\n\r\n</html>\r\n</div><br /><hr><br /><div><html>\r\n\r\n<head>\r\n<title>Rule 67:46:13:11 Ineligibility for fraud.</title>\r\n<META NAME=\"Keywords\" Content=\"Administrative Rules 67:46:13:11\">\r\n<META NAME=\"Description\" Content=\"Administrative Rules 67:46:13:11 Ineligibility for fraud.\">\r\n<meta http-equiv=Content-Type content=\"text/html; charset=windows-1252\">\r\n<meta name=Generator content=\"Microsoft Word 14 (filtered)\">\r\n<style>\r\n<!--\r\n /* Font Definitions */\r\n @font-face\r\n\t{font-family:Calibri;\r\n\tpanose-1:2 15 5 2 2 2 4 3 2 4;}\r\n /* Style Definitions */\r\n p.MsoNormal, li.MsoNormal, div.MsoNormal\r\n\t{margin:0in;\r\n\tmargin-bottom:.0001pt;\r\n\ttext-align:justify;\r\n\tfont-size:12.0pt;\r\n\tfont-family:\"Times New Roman\",\"serif\";}\r\n@page WordSection1\r\n\t{size:8.5in 11.0in;\r\n\tmargin:1.0in 1.0in 1.0in 1.0in;}\r\ndiv.WordSection1\r\n\t{page:WordSection1;}\r\n-->\r\n</style>\r\n\r\n</head>\r\n\r\n<body lang=EN-US>\r\n\r\n<div class=WordSection1>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; <b>67:46:13:11.&nbsp;&nbsp;Ineligibility for\r\nfraud.</b> If a court of law finds that a member of a Medicaid household\r\ncommitted fraud resulting in mistaken eligibility for Medicaid for one of the\r\nsix months preceding the current period of Medicaid ineligibility, all members\r\nof the Medicaid household in which the fraud was committed are ineligible for\r\ncontinued medical coverage under this chapter.</p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; <b>Source:</b> 24 SDR 24, effective August 31,\r\n1997; 41 SDR 7, effective July 29, 2014.</p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; <b>General Authority:</b> SDCL <A HREF=\"/statutes/DisplayStatute.aspx?Type=Statute&Statute=28-6-1\">28-6-1.</A></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; <b>Law Implemented:</b> SDCL <A HREF=\"/statutes/DisplayStatute.aspx?Type=Statute&Statute=28-6-1\">28-6-1.</A></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=MsoNormal>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n</body>\r\n\r\n</html>\r\n</div>",
